In the lecture the continuity of a function at a point \(c\) was characterized by the following sequence criterion:

\[
\boxed{\;f \text{ is continuous at } c \;\Longleftrightarrow\; 
\text{for every sequence }(x_n)\subset S \text{ with } x_n\to c,\;
\lim_{n\to\infty}f(x_n)=f(c).\;}
\]

In other words, \(f\) is continuous at \(c\) exactly when every sequence of points from the domain that converges to \(c\) produces a sequence of function values that converges to \(f(c)\).

